eded by a later modification.\n\nWhat we would like from you: when you are trying to understand what a permit actually requires for a given monitoring period, how do you use these package documents? Is there a reliable hierarchy — for instance, does the final permit generally control over a fact sheet or statement of basis, and does a minor modification override what came before? Or does authority depend on something we cannot see from filenames alone, like issuance dates or explicit cross-references inside the text?\n\nAnd separately: even knowing that the PDFs exist but not having their text in hand — is \"we cannot establish narrative conditions from structured sources alone\" the right place to stop, or would you treat certain document kinds as strong enough signals on their own to draw limited conclusions without opening every file?\n\nWe are not asking you to quote permit language. We want your professional judgment on whether our stop point is sensible, whether we are worrying about the right documents, or whether we are missing a distinction you would always make in practice.\n","isEmpty":false,"exceededLimit":false,"totalLines":14,"fileSize":2847,"path":"/tmp/world-experiment/npdes-conversational-semantic-review-v1/9dd815d429ff63476904edda6bf0fbf4/HOST_MESSAGE.md","readRange":{"startLine":1,"endLine":14},"relatedCursorRulePaths":[],"relatedCursorRules":[]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_8b8fc861-de38-4844-bf82-51896f45c43","startedAtMs":"1788592378127","completedAtMs":"1788592378531"},"model_call_id":"053a306e-35ac-4aca-b662-eba5a51c1f0f-0-lhbm","session_id":"c3ed1518-faf5-4f4b-903c-90c52944650e","timestamp_ms":1788592378558}
